WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.801
Step 1. Open the Appointments page.

1.2
00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:07.466
Here you find appointments and open them in Appointment Details.

1.3
00:00:07.466 --> 00:00:13.140
In the facility sidebar, under Patient Management, select Appointments.

2.1
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:18.845
Step 2. Choose a view. The Appointments page opens on the Board view.

2.2
00:00:18.845 --> 00:00:22.191
To see a table instead, select List.

3.1
00:00:22.191 --> 00:00:24.703
Step 3. Filter the appointments.

3.2
00:00:24.703 --> 00:00:30.218
The Practitioners filter starts with you, and its list shows your departments.

3.3
00:00:30.218 --> 00:00:36.375
Here you add Dr. Meera Iyer. The tags and the date range are in the filter menu.

4.1
00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:40.342
Step 4. Turn on auto refresh. This step is optional.

4.2
00:00:40.342 --> 00:00:44.702
Turn on Auto Refresh to refresh the page at a fixed interval,

4.3
00:00:44.702 --> 00:00:49.919
every 10 seconds unless your deployment sets a different interval.

5.1
00:00:49.919 --> 00:00:52.837
Step 5. Read the board or the list.

5.2
00:00:52.837 --> 00:00:57.564
The board has the columns Booked, Checked-In, In-Consultation,

5.3
00:00:57.564 --> 00:01:03.858
Fulfilled and Non Fulfilled. The list has a tab for each of the same groups.

6.1
00:01:03.858 --> 00:01:10.398
Step 6. Open an appointment. Select a card on the board, or a row in the list.

6.2
00:01:10.398 --> 00:01:13.397
Care opens Appointment Details.

7.1
00:01:13.397 --> 00:01:16.102
Step 7. Read Appointment Details.

7.2
00:01:16.102 --> 00:01:21.457
Schedule Information shows the status, date, session, time and duration.

7.3
00:01:21.457 --> 00:01:27.184
Which Quick Actions show depends on the status and on whether an encounter is

7.4
00:01:27.184 --> 00:01:28.204
linked.
